SCOPE: DI2 shared periods, civil clock/history, forecast eligibility and
consumer parity. No DI3/DI4 layout requirements, year AddDate policy change,
source fixes, git-state changes, subagents or ledger edits. Lead gates.

F1 — New year-control history check compares raw instants to civil bounds.
Criteria: task-2-brief.md calendar-day/DST-safe logic and consistent full/HTMX
adapters; approved design Periods, comparisons and freshness (civil dates and
truthful history availability). Location: internal/handlers/dashboard/period.go:32.
BuildPeriodContext normalizes evidence dates to civil midnight; dashboardPeriod
overwrites its history availability for comparison=year using raw MinDate and
MaxDate against normalized PreviousStart/PreviousEnd. A transaction on the
first prior calendar day can therefore incorrectly fail the coverage test.

Exact synthetic reproduction:
- Now 2026-03-06; selected 2026-02-01..2026-02-28; comparison=year.
- Prior row: 2025-02-01 12:00 UTC, $100 outflow.
- Current row: 2026-02-28 12:00 UTC, $200 outflow.
- Prior bounds remain exactly 2025-02-01..2025-02-28. No leap-day fixture.
- Got HistoryAvailable=false; dashboardPeriodComparison.HasData=false;
  shared/period-context renders 'Not enough history to compare'. The $100
  prior comparison is suppressed despite civil evidence bounds enclosing it.
- Midnight UTC on the same first day passes. UTC noon, west-offset midnight
  and noon, and east-offset noon fail. East-offset midnight passes the new
  check. The difference is raw instant comparison, not missing evidence.

Fresh executable evidence in /tmp/DI2-second.ArN3VU:
rtk proxy go test ./internal/handlers/dashboard -run '^TestDI2SecondYear' -v -count=1
Exit 1. TestDI2SecondYearCivilHistory fails four of six time/zone variants;
TestDI2SecondYearHistoryRendered fails on the actual rendered false statement.
Probe retained at internal/handlers/dashboard/di2_second_year_test.go in copy.
The candidate was raised by the lead and independently executed/confirmed here.

Premise and remedy checked:
- The unchanged legacy metrics.Comparison returns HasData=true, prior $100
  for the UTC-noon fixture. Compared metrics/metrics.go to immutable baseline
  with cmp: identical. Thus the concrete UTC-noon failure is newly introduced,
  not the prior year-range normalization behavior.
- Test changes only the generated PeriodContext's availability/reason metadata
  in memory (not source, dates, transactions or bounds). The same real adapter
  then returns prior $100 and real context rendering removes the false message.
  Remedy is consistent civil-date history evaluation in this new override;
  changing year AddDate or hiding only the text would not repair the cause.

